D(10,'RF_S1E10_A16',[('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie',"Who's holding those vents?"),('OFFICER','Officer','Scythe.'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','And the locks?'),('OFFICER','Officer','Triarch code confirmed.'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','All right. Off the doors. Ten klicks.'),('OFFICER','Officer','Triarch ordered—'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','I heard them.')]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A16',"Billie receives the same proof packet while Ashfang is still crowding the evac bays. She asks enough questions to make sure the sabotage is real, then orders her ship back. Her officer invokes the Triarch; Billie cuts the argument off and executes the retreat.")
no_dialogue(10,'RF_S1E10_A17'); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A17',"Inside Shatterforge, the pressure release changes the evacuation physically: doors that were bowed shut crack open, smoke reverses direction, and crews pull families out of the lower runs. The relief is temporary; heat still climbs on Scythe's side of the system.")
D(10,'RF_S1E10_A18',[('ENGINEER','Engineer','Dorsal lattice goes in twenty seconds.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','How many skiffs left?'),('ENGINEER','Engineer','Three.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Then give them twenty.')]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A18',"Cracks spread across Scythe's bridge glass and warning strips go white-hot. The engineer reports the ship's remaining tolerance. Abby looks not at the damage but at the evac count on another display. Three skiffs are still inside; her answer is tied directly to that number.")
no_dialogue(10,'RF_S1E10_A19'); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A19',"Gravefire bursts from the smoke towing the last chain of evacuation skiffs. One skiff is visibly damaged and riding almost against Gravefire's hull. Thunderbreak's shield overlap reaches them as Scythe's silhouette disappears deeper in the furnace bloom.")
D(10,'RF_S1E10_A20',[('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical','Civilians coming out. Ashfang backed off.'),('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical',"Pike's still in the plume."),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Forget Pike. Cover the skiffs.')]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A20',"On Thunderbreak, Tactical reports three changing facts while Venn is allocating shield arcs. Pike's broadcast icon flashes for attention; Venn closes it and spends the power on the evacuation corridor. Exterior: the shield catches the damaged skiff.")
no_dialogue(10,'RF_S1E10_A21'); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A21',"A furnace jet catches Broken Oath broadside while Pike is still too close. His ceremonial broadcast cloak and external banners burn away first, then armor scorches. The camera drones tumble out of formation. The visual punctures the performance without needing a joke.")
D(10,'RF_S1E10_A22',[('@starsplit.oren.pike','Pike','Who put us this close?'),('OFFICER','Officer','You did.'),('@starsplit.oren.pike','Pike','Right. Move us.')]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A22',"Sparks rain across Broken Oath's bridge after the heat strike. Pike demands an answer before the officer can stop himself from giving the obvious one. Pike absorbs it, drops the performance, and orders an actual retreat.")
D(10,'RF_S1E10_A23',[('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Venn. Record packet coming.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Receiving.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Vent locks were Triarch. Deliberate.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Are the skiffs clear?'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Last one just crossed.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Good.')]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A23',"Scythe's transmission is breaking up as Abby pushes the sabotage packet to Thunderbreak. She gets the evidence out first, then asks the only question she cannot see from inside the furnace plume: whether the last skiffs are clear. Venn checks the live lane and answers. Abby's final 'Good' is cut by static, not followed by a farewell.")
no_dialogue(10,'RF_S1E10_A24'); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A24',"Scythe disappears behind a white furnace bloom. Its transponder flickers once, then vanishes from every nearby tactical screen. Do not show an explosion that proves destruction; preserve ambiguity.")
no_dialogue(10,'RF_S1E10_A25'); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A25',"At dusk, the evacuation skiffs climb out under Fleet shields while Shard ships hold off instead of attacking. Families look back at the smoke column over Shatterforge. Broken Oath limps away scorched; Ashfang remains outside the bays.")
D(10,'RF_S1E10_A26',[('HELM','Helm','Scythe transponder?'),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','No.'),('HELM','Helm','You think—'),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','Dock the civilians.')]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A26',"On Gravefire, the helm officer keeps searching for Scythe while Tess watches the same blank sector. She answers the factual question, refuses the speculative one, and redirects the bridge to docking the rescued people.")
D(10,'RF_S1E10_A27',[('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical','Last civilian skiff is clear.'),('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical','Scythe still no transponder.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn',"Mark her unaccounted. Attach Abby's packet to the incident record.")]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A27',"Thunderbreak's board settles from emergency red to ordinary status except for one blank Scythe identifier. Venn does not pronounce Abby dead. She changes the status to UNACCOUNTED and links the sabotage evidence to the official incident file.")
D(10,'RF_S1E10_A28',[('@starsplit.halev','Halev','She put the whole ship in the vent.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','Yeah.'),('@starsplit.jex.marrin','Jex','And the account that bought the locks is in the packet.'),('@starsplit.halev','Halev','Make another copy.'),('@starsplit.jex.marrin','Jex','Already making six.')]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A28',"Halev, Naomi and Jex listen to Venn's report while the first evacuees arrive on Auric dock cameras. Halev is stuck on the image of Scythe in the plume. Jex returns the room to the evidence and begins duplicating the packet again. Naomi says almost nothing because she is watching survivors step off the skiffs.")
D(10,'RF_S1E10_A29',[('TRIARCH','Triarch','Auric Gate.'),('@starsplit.emissary','Emissary','After this?'),('TRIARCH','Triarch','Because of this.')]); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A29',"The Triarch watch Abby's sabotage proof spreading across public feeds. Rather than retreat, they pull up the Auric Gate plan. An emissary hesitates for the first time. On a separate feed, Billie receives the same order and does not acknowledge it.")
no_dialogue(10,'RF_S1E10_A30'); set_direction(10,'RF_S1E10_A30',"Night aftermath over Shatterforge: smoke tears sideways in the wind; emergency vents are finally open; families crowd temporary shelters. Deep in the furnace haze, a tiny irregular engine flicker appears once and is obscured again. Do not identify it.")

# ISSUE 11
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A01'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A01',"Dawn at the Auric Gate. Civilian traffic is already moving when Shard contacts begin appearing beyond the pylons. Keep cargo skiffs and ordinary commuters visible beneath the scale of the gathering fleets; the battle is arriving at a functioning road.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A02',[('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical','Shard massing. Broken Oath. Ashfang. Triarch hulls behind them.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Civilian count?'),('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical','Twenty-three in the approach.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Keep them moving.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A02',"Thunderbreak's threat board fills with incoming Shard signatures. Venn asks for the civilian count before giving a battle order. Tactical overlays twenty-three civilian hulls already committed to the approach; Venn keeps the lane active and rotates shields outward.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A03',[('@starsplit.oren.pike','Pike','Open every channel.'),('OFFICER','Officer','Even civilian?'),('@starsplit.oren.pike','Pike','Especially civilian.'),('@starsplit.oren.pike','Pike',"If we're taking the Gate, I want witnesses.")]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A03',"Pike brings Broken Oath forward with replacement banners and camera drones hastily mounted after Shatterforge. His officer hesitates over the civilian bands. Pike deliberately opens them too and broadcasts his approach before any shot is fired.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A04',[('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','Crown hulls only.'),('OFFICER','Officer',"Pike's painting the whole lane."),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','Then Pike can shoot by himself.'),('OFFICER','Officer','Triarch says burn the Gate.'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','I heard them too.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A04',"On Ashfang, target boxes begin appearing over both Fleet ships and civilian traffic because Pike's shared feed is indiscriminate. Billie clears every civilian box from her board and orders her crew to target only armed Crown hulls. The Triarch order is visible but unacknowledged.")
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A05'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A05',"Fleet shields lock around the Gate while the civilian lane remains open through the middle. The formation is therefore imperfect by military standards: ships are leaving gaps to let traffic through. Shard fire begins testing those gaps.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A06',[('@starsplit.halev','Halev','How long if the Gate shuts?'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','To reroute everything?'),('@starsplit.halev','Halev','Yeah.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','Long enough to hurt.'),('@starsplit.halev','Halev',"Then don't chase them. Keep the road.")]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A06',"Halev is in Gate control with the civilian queue stretching across his screens. Naomi is already strapped into Sunlash. He asks for the consequence in practical terms, gets the answer, and makes the mission simple: the escorts stay with traffic even while a battle forms around them.")
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A07'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A07',"Broken Oath charges through Gate midspace, weaving between pylon fire and civilian vectors to keep itself centered in the public feeds. Pike's maneuver forces both Fleet and Verge pilots to alter course around him.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A08',[('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical','Ashfang closing. Impact vector.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Prow shields.'),('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical','Fire solution is clean.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Not with those skiffs behind her.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A08',"Tactical presents a clean shot on Ashfang, but the wider display shows civilian skiffs beyond Billie's vector. Venn orders prow shields instead. Thunderbreak absorbs the approach while gunnery crews watch a legal target pass through an unsafe background.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A09',[('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess',"Skiff Four, you're outside me."),('PILOT','Pilot',"I can't see the marker."),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','Forget the marker. See Gravefire?'),('PILOT','Pilot','Yeah.'),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','Follow me.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A09',"Gate fire and distortion obscure the lane markers for one civilian skiff. Tess uses Gravefire itself as the reference point and brings the pilot into Fleet shadow. The scene is a flying problem in the middle of the battle, not a calming speech.")
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A10'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A10',"Pike fires through the edge of the civilian lane to hit a Fleet escort. The shot misses the skiffs by an unacceptable margin and one civilian craft spins from the shock wave. Broken Oath's public cameras capture the near hit along with the attack Pike intended to celebrate.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A11',[('TRIARCH','Triarch','Burn the Gate.'),('@starsplit.emissary','Emissary','Civilian traffic is still inside.'),('TRIARCH','Triarch','Burn it.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A11',"In the Arena Vault, the Triarch see the same civilian-lane overlay as everyone else. The emissary points to the occupied Gate before repeating the concern. The second order comes with full knowledge of who is inside.")
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A12'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A12',"The Rift shudders under overlapping weapons fire and Gate stabilization pulses. Duplicate ships begin appearing at the edges of synchronized formations—first one, then several. Targeting systems multiply boxes faster than crews can identify real hulls.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A13',[('@starsplit.jia.morgan','Jia','Venn, stop the synchronized fire.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Why?'),('@starsplit.jia.morgan','Jia','Every volley gives the copies the same pattern.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','All batteries cold.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Naomi, I need your hands.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','You have them.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A13',"Jia overlays the Gate battle with the Calm Corridor telemetry and sees duplicate density spike after synchronized volleys. She calls Venn directly. Venn asks the necessary question, then shuts Thunderbreak's batteries down and calls Naomi. Across the lane, Verge hand signs begin replacing targeting clocks.")
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A14'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A14',"A scarred, partially blackened Scythe of Saville emerges from the outer Rift with jury-rigged thrust. Several Shard ships fall in behind it. Inside damaged viewports, survivors are visible. The return should be unmistakable before any character names Abby.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A15',[('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby',"If you're still with me, shields on the convoys."),('CAPTAIN','Captain','Triarch is ordering the Gate burned.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','I know.'),('CAPTAIN','Captain',"That's the break, then?"),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Looks like.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A15',"Abby opens a channel to the captains who followed Scythe out of Shatterforge. One captain asks the question nobody has yet said aloud while their ships face the Triarch formation. Abby answers almost tiredly, then turns Scythe's remaining shield power toward the civilian lane. The other captains follow one by one.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A16',[('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','Billie. Pike just fired through a skiff.'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','I saw.'),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','You still with him?'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','Shut up.'),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','Okay.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A16',"Tess calls Billie while both are still flying combat vectors. On Billie's board, Pike's shot replay shows the civilian near miss. Tess does not tell Billie what kind of person she is; she asks whether Billie is still choosing Pike's side. Billie has no clean answer and ends the conversation herself.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A17',[('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Thunderbreak, break target lock.'),('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical','All batteries?'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','All.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Put everything into the civilian shield.'),('@starsplit.tactical','Tactical',"We'll be open."),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','I know.')]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A17',"Venn does not give a ceasefire speech to every faction. She orders her own ship first. Target boxes vanish from Thunderbreak; weapon power pours into the civilian shield; the cruiser becomes visibly vulnerable. Nearby Fleet ships see what Thunderbreak has done and begin following without being told. Naomi's escorts are already on convoy geometry; Abby's bloc is already shielding. The ceasefire becomes legible through ships changing behavior.")
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A17B',[('@starsplit.oren.pike','Pike',"They're open! Fire!"),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','Pike.'),('@starsplit.oren.pike','Pike','What?'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','Move.'),('@starsplit.oren.pike','Pike',"I'm taking the Gate."),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie',"No. You're blocking my shot.")]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A17B',"Pike keeps firing after surrounding ships begin dropping target locks. Billie lines Ashfang up behind Broken Oath and tells him to move. Pike assumes she wants his firing lane and refuses. Billie's last line is true only in the most literal sense: her shot is aimed at Broken Oath's weapon mast. She fires and disables it without destroying the ship."); set_panelplan(11,'RF_S1E11_A17B',['Broken Oath continues firing while target boxes disappear from ships around it.','Billie lines Ashfang up behind Pike and tells him to move.','Pike, ecstatic, says he is taking the Gate and refuses.',"Billie: 'No. You're blocking my shot.' Her reticle is now clearly on Broken Oath's weapon mast.","Ashfang fires. Broken Oath's mast dies; the ship survives, suddenly unable to continue the massacre."])
D(11,'RF_S1E11_A18',[('@starsplit.selene.stormwell','Selene','Verge escorts dropped target lock first.'),('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','Thunderbreak followed.'),('@starsplit.selene.stormwell','Selene',"Then Saville's ships."),('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','And the Gate held.'),('@starsplit.selene.stormwell','Selene',"I'll record all four.")]); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A18',"Selene and Dominion reconstruct the sequence from timestamped combat logs after the firing stops. They are not debating the meaning of restraint; they are establishing what happened and in what order. Selene includes the Gate's survival as well as every faction's choice.")
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A19'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A19',"Dawn after the battle. Convoys still thread the Gate through wreckage and disabled ships. Mixed crews tow damaged civilian hulls without checking faction markings first. Broken Oath drifts powerless but intact; Ashfang keeps its distance.")
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A20'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A20',"On Gravefire, Tess watches the last delayed civilian skiff clear the Gate. She removes her headset and rubs the pressure mark behind one ear while the bridge crew quietly starts damage checks. No line is needed.")
no_dialogue(11,'RF_S1E11_A21'); set_direction(11,'RF_S1E11_A21',"Wide orbit: Auric Gate still functions, scarred pylons pulsing unevenly as ordinary traffic resumes. The surviving ships sit in awkward mixed positions around it—no clean victory formation. End on the road remaining open.")

# ISSUE 12
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A01',[('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','The ceasefire expires at 0600.'),('@starsplit.halev','Halev','Then we have four hours.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','To do what?'),('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','Decide whether it expires.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A01',"The Relic Court opens with the ceasefire clock visible on the wall and the Auric Gate traffic feed still running beside it. Dominion is not giving a closing speech; he states the deadline. Halev checks the clock. Venn makes him say what the meeting is actually for.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A02',[('@starsplit.jex.marrin','Jex','Before anybody decides anything—page fourteen.'),('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','What am I looking at?'),('@starsplit.jex.marrin','Jex','Same account tree. Shortage buys, the man who stabbed me, Shatterforge vent relays.'),('@starsplit.halev','Halev','Copies?'),('@starsplit.jex.marrin','Jex',"Enough that killing me would be a waste of everyone's morning.")]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A02',"Jex arrives late enough to interrupt the formal opening and slides physical ledger copies down the court table. He opens Dominion's copy to page fourteen himself. The transaction tree is visible beside the sabotage packet from Abby. Halev asks the practical preservation question while Jex is still distributing copies.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A03',[('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','You want Shard ships inside Fleet beacon control.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','My ships were inside your shield at the Gate.'),('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','During a battle.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Yeah. It was inconvenient.'),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','Still worked.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A03',"Dominion highlights the mixed-escort clause on the draft. Abby answers by pulling up the Gate replay showing her ships physically inside Fleet shield geometry. Dominion distinguishes emergency from policy; Abby refuses to romanticize the emergency. Tess contributes only the observable result.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A04',[('@starsplit.halev','Halev','If Verge crews fly the route, Verge gets a say before somebody closes it.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Agreed.'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie',"No, it isn't."),('@starsplit.halev','Halev','Billie.'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie',"Page three. 'Fleet timing authority.' You agreed to nothing.")]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A04',"Halev is negotiating the closure clause with Venn when Billie walks in uninvited, takes a draft from an aide, and immediately finds the timing language. She interrupts because the text contradicts the verbal agreement happening in front of her. Everyone's attention moves from Billie to the actual line on page three.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A05',[('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','Fleet clock. Fleet beacons. Fleet decides when everybody\'s late.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby',"She's right."),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','The Gate still needs one clock.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi',"One clock isn't the same as one owner."),('@starsplit.halev','Halev','Change it to shared timing.'),('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','Defined how?'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','Two parties publish the mark. Same as a closure.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A05',"Billie taps the three Fleet-controlled terms one by one on the draft. Abby backs the objection before Venn can defend the wording. Naomi reaches across and rewrites 'Fleet timing authority' as 'shared timing' on the projected document. Dominion makes her define the mechanism; she does it in the same operational terms they already use at the Gate."); set_panelplan(12,'RF_S1E12_A05',['Billie stands over the draft and points to three separate Fleet-control clauses while naming them.',"Abby says Billie is right. Venn points to the single Gate clock on the live feed and says the system still needs one.","Naomi: 'One clock isn't the same as one owner.'",'Halev tells the clerk to change the wording to shared timing.','Dominion asks how that actually works. Naomi writes the two-party publication rule into the draft.'])
no_dialogue(12,'RF_S1E12_A06'); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A06',"Billie drops a Shard coin on the draft to hold down page three while the clerk makes the change. She does not sit. The coin remains on the page through the next round of edits, a practical marker of the objection she forced into the room.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A07',[('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Published windows. Mixed escorts. Weapons cold inside the civilian perimeter unless fired on.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi',"No. 'Unless fired on' starts an argument every time somebody sees a ghost."),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Fair. No first fire.'),('@starsplit.halev','Halev','Civilian cargo before military repositioning.'),('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','Emergency closure?'),('@starsplit.halev','Halev','Two parties.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','Unless the Gate itself is failing.'),('@starsplit.selene.stormwell','Selene','For the memorial record: names without faction rank.'),('@starsplit.cael.dominion','Dominion','Thirty days. Auric Gate only.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby',"Thirty days is enough to find out if we're lying.")]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A07',"The Accord is written in real time on a shared projected draft. Venn reads a clause; Naomi catches dangerous ambiguity and edits it. Halev adds cargo priority. Dominion tests the failure case. Selene waits until the operational terms are settled before adding the memorial-record language. Dominion limits the trial by physically entering '30 DAYS / AURIC GATE ONLY.' The scene should look like people working on a document, not taking turns delivering principles.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A08',[('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Thirty days.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby',"Don't waste them."),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn',"Wasn't planning to."),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Good.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A08',"After the larger room breaks into clerks and signatures, Venn and Abby meet at the edge of the table over the final thirty-day line. Neither offers reconciliation. They confirm the time they have bought and separate to their own people.")
no_dialogue(12,'RF_S1E12_A09'); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A09',"Dusk at Auric Gate. New shared-timing markers replace the old Fleet-only labels on the control displays. Verge, Fleet and Abby-aligned Shard crews are all physically present at the launch board, awkwardly sharing the same countdown.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A10',[('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Green One, shared mark in ten.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','Verge confirms.'),('@starsplit.abby.saville','Abby','Shard escort confirms.'),('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Mark.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A10',"The first Accord convoy waits at the line. Venn calls the countdown from Thunderbreak, but Naomi and Abby each confirm the same mark from their own ships before Venn releases it. The convoy moves only after all three confirmations are visible.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A11',[('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi',"Blue Two, don't bunch up just because we have company."),('PILOT','Pilot','Trying to be friendly.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','Try flying.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A11',"On Sunlash, one Verge escort drifts too close to a Shard partner while everyone is hyper-aware of the new mixed formation. Naomi corrects the spacing and punctures the pilot's nervous attempt at friendliness. The ships settle into a workable distance.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A12',[('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','Same mark. Keep your own spacing.'),('SHARD PILOT','Shard Pilot',"Fleet's early."),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess',"No. You're late.")]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A12',"On Gravefire, Tess watches a Shard escort misread the shared clock and blame the Fleet. She checks the mark, corrects the pilot, and keeps the formation moving. Cooperation looks like mundane correction, not harmony.")
no_dialogue(12,'RF_S1E12_A13'); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A13',"The First Memorial Convoy passes through the Gate under genuinely mixed escort. Civilian cargo is visibly ahead of military repositioning ships waiting their turn. The route works, but the formation is still visually heterogeneous and slightly awkward.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A14',[('TRIARCH','Triarch','One Gate.'),('TRIARCH','Triarch','Thirty days.'),('@starsplit.emissary','Emissary','You want us to wait?'),('TRIARCH','Triarch','Yes.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A14',"In the mostly empty Arena Vault, the Triarch read the Accord terms without public theatrics. One mask taps the one-Gate limitation; another the thirty-day expiration. The emissary asks whether the response is simply to wait. The answer is yes, which is more threatening than another immediate attack.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A15',[('OFFICER','Officer','They changed the timing clause.'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','I saw.'),('OFFICER','Officer','You signing now?'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie','No.'),('OFFICER','Officer','Why not?'),('@starsplit.billie.rusk','Billie',"Because I don't want to.")]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A15',"Billie watches the shared convoy from Ashfang outside the Accord formation. An officer notes that her objection actually changed the document and asks the obvious follow-up. Billie refuses for the most personal reason possible. She stays outside without attacking the lane.")
no_dialogue(12,'RF_S1E12_A16'); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A16',"In the Relic Court after hours, Selene enters the day's memorial record. There are no names to add for deaths inside the corridor. She checks the blank line twice, then closes the register without a speech.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A17',[('@starsplit.jex.marrin','Jex','I have a new policy.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','That sounds expensive.'),('@starsplit.jex.marrin','Jex','Truth first.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','How much?'),('@starsplit.jex.marrin','Jex','Introductory rate.'),('@starsplit.naomi.sol','Naomi','There it is.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A17',"Jex is helping unload newly arrived crates at Auric because his staff are overwhelmed, which makes his announcement less grand than he wants. Naomi opens a crate beside him while asking the inevitable price question. Jex cannot resist monetizing the joke even after the season he has had.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A18',[('@starsplit.child','Kid','Captain?'),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','Yeah?'),('@starsplit.child','Kid','Did we win?'),('@starsplit.tessa.banks','Tess','We got home.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A18',"Tess sits in Gravefire's quiet berth while a child from the convoy waits for a parent finishing intake paperwork. The child asks the question without ceremony. Tess looks through the open hatch at the dock they actually reached and gives the smallest truthful answer she has.")
no_dialogue(12,'RF_S1E12_A19'); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A19',"At dawn, the second Accord convoy forms with less hesitation than the first. Crews still check one another's clocks, but nobody needs to explain the shared procedure. Civilian freighters take the front positions while military ships wait behind.")
D(12,'RF_S1E12_A20',[('@starsplit.ella.venn','Venn','Open the next window.')]); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A20',"On Thunderbreak, the Gate clock reaches the scheduled mark. Venn checks the shared confirmations already lit from Verge and Shard control, then gives the ordinary order to open the next window. The achievement is that the line sounds routine.")
no_dialogue(12,'RF_S1E12_A21'); set_direction(12,'RF_S1E12_A21',"Wide orbit. The second convoy threads the lane while unrelated traffic waits, turns and resumes around it. No victory tableau and no closing narration. The system is functioning, provisionally, because people are using it.")

# Exact coverage and mechanical-reference checks built into the transform itself.
for n, data in rew.items():
    expected = {s['id'] for s in data}
    actual = {sid for issue, sid in touched if issue == n}
    if actual != expected:
        raise SystemExit(f'Issue {n}: scene coverage mismatch; missing={sorted(expected-actual)}; extra={sorted(actual-expected)}')

characters = json.loads((ROOT/'characters.json').read_text())
valid_handles = set()
for c in characters.values():
    if c.get('handle'): valid_handles.add(c['handle'])
    valid_handles.update(c.get('aliases') or [])
for n, data in rew.items():
    for s in data:
        for d in s.get('dialogueInline') or []:
            h = d.get('handle')
            if isinstance(h,str) and h.startswith('@') and h not in valid_handles:
                raise SystemExit(f'Issue {n} {s["id"]}: unresolved dialogue handle {h}')

expected_counts={2:27,3:30,4:31,5:21,6:15,7:19,8:12,9:15,10:30,11:22,12:21}
for n,data in rew.items():
    if len(data) != expected_counts[n]: raise SystemExit(f'Issue {n}: expected {expected_counts[n]} scenes, found {len(data)}')
    if len({s['id'] for s in data}) != len(data): raise SystemExit(f'Issue {n}: duplicate scene id')
for n,data in rew.items(): save_issue(n,data)
print('Applied comic-writing rewrite to Issues 2-12: 243 scenes addressed.')
